            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0380" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856d.6363/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-06T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>587. Your 254 September 15 and Department’s 573 September 22. Telegraph results
                    of conversation with Foreign Office regarding intention of Secretary of Interior
                    to exclude Netherlands citizens <pb facs="0381" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/> from
                    American public lands. Prompt action is necessary in order that consideration
                    may be given to more definite counter measures. Have you asked for joint
                    American participation in Djambi concession?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
